00:05:07,058 --> 00:05:13,058
Welcome to the future

2
00:10:14,117 --> 00:10:20,117
Generation X is a tv movie, action, fantasy film directed by Jack Sholder.

3
00:15:21,176 --> 00:15:27,176
A group of young mutants--humans with a genetic variation that gives them superpowers and makes
them feared by the population at large--begin training at a school for heroes.

4
00:20:28,235 --> 00:20:34,235
Their studies are interrupted when they must rescue one of their
number from a mad scientist who can enter others' dreams.

5
00:25:35,294 --> 00:25:41,294
Russel Tresh, played by Matt Frewer.

6
00:30:42,352 --> 00:30:48,352
Emma Frost, played by Finola Hughes.

7
00:35:49,411 --> 00:35:55,411
Sean Cassidy, played by Jeremy Ratchford.

8
00:40:56,470 --> 00:41:02,470
Jubilation Lee / Jubilee, played by Heather McComb.

9
00:46:03,529 --> 00:46:09,529
Angelo Espinosa / Skin, played by Agustin Rodriguez.

10
00:51:10,588 --> 00:51:16,588
Kurt Pastorius, played by Randall Slavin.

11
00:56:17,647 --> 00:56:23,647
Generation X is a television pilot directed by Jack
Sholder that aired on Fox on February 20, 1996.

12
01:01:24,705 --> 01:01:30,705
It was later broadcast as a television film.

13
01:06:31,764 --> 01:06:37,764
It is based on the Marvel comic book series of the same
name, a spin-off of the X-Men franchise.

14
01:11:38,823 --> 01:11:44,823
It was produced by New World Entertainment and Marvel Entertainment Group.

15
01:16:45,882 --> 01:16:51,882
The film explores themes of superhero, mutant, based on comic, super power.

16
01:21:52,941 --> 01:21:58,941
The tone is thought_provoking.
